            <ArticleTitle>A large intracardiac thrombus in a child with steroid-resistant nephrotic syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>440-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951112000923</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intracardiac thrombus is a rare complication of nephrotic syndrome in children, and only a few cases have been reported. We report the case of a 3.5-year-old child diagnosed with Henoch-Schönlein Purpura and steroid-resistant nephrotic syndrome for 2 months. The patient had massive oedema but no cardiovascular instability. Echocardiography displayed a large thrombus within the right atrium and the patient was successfully managed with enoxoparine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
